# energy-efficient-smart-street-light

Energy-efficient hybrid smart street lighting system using solar and wind energy with Arduino Uno, LDR and IR sensors.

## Overview

This project implements an energy-efficient hybrid street lighting system using solar and wind energy.
The system uses Arduino Uno, LDR and IR sensors to automatically control LED street lights based on ambient light and motion detection.
The renewable energy generated is stored in a rechargeable battery for reliable off-grid operation.

## Features

- Solar and wind energy generation
- Automatic street light control
- LDR based light detection
- IR based motion detection
- Arduino Uno implementation
- Rechargeable battery storage
- Energy-efficient LED lighting
- Off-grid operation

## Tools Used

- Arduino Uno
- LDR Sensor
- IR Sensor
- Solar Panel
- Wind Turbine
- Relay Module
- Rechargeable Battery
- Voltage Regulator
- Diode
- LED Lights

## Files

- Block diagram
- Hardware setup
- Output results
- Flow / system description

## Applications

- Smart city street lighting
- Renewable energy systems
- Rural and remote area lighting
- Off-grid lighting
- Energy-efficient public infrastructure

## Output

The system successfully controls the LED street lights based on LDR and IR sensor inputs.
When the LDR detects the required light condition and the IR sensor detects an object, the LEDs are activated.
The hybrid solar and wind energy system provides power while the rechargeable battery supports continuous operation.
